    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d748">

                <pb facs="0689" n="573" xml:id="pg573"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.51/219.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Honduras to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of Honduras</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-02-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 20, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Pursuant to the convention dated January
                    10, 1911, between the Republic of Honduras and the United States of America, I
                    have, on behalf of my Government and in accordance with its instructions, made
                    and executed with an American banking group, consisting of J. P. Morgan &amp;
                    Co., Kuhn, Loeb &amp; Co., the National City Bank of New York, and the First
                    National Bank of New York, a loan contract, dated February 15, 1911; and with
                    the Guaranty Trust Company of New York, as fiscal agent, a contract securing the
                    said loan, dated the same day; both contracts being in the form already
                    submitted to and approved by your Department. In accordance with the
                    requirements of said contracts, I accompany an original executed counterpart of
                    each contract<anchor n="1" xml:id="d748-f1"/> in English and in Spanish, to be
                    filed with the Department of State of the United States of America.</p>
                <p>Kindly acknowledge the receipt of the said contracts as executed and filed in
                    conformity to said convention.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Luis Lazo A.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
